(Title) Tj
T*
(Incidence and Timing of Heel Ulceration Across Acute Care Settings: A Pathway Analysis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(We prospectively followed 183 hospitalized patients with neurological or functional) Tj
T*
(impairments across pre-hospital transport, emergency care, and hospital wards at two) Tj
T*
(Swedish academic centers. One group \(91 patients\) received a protective heel device) Tj
T*
(beginning in the ambulance; 92 controls received routine care. Among the entire cohort, 38) Tj
T*
(individuals \(21%\) developed heel tissue breakdown at various points in the care pathway.) Tj
T*
(In the device group, 18% developed tissue injury compared to 24% in controls. The majority) Tj
T*
(of pressure-related damage occurred during the ward phase \(59% of all cases\), though early) Tj
T*
(signs were detected in 12% of patients during emergency department evaluation. Univariate) Tj
T*
(analysis identified admission severity score, duration of bed rest, and delayed mobility) Tj
T*
(as predictive of tissue breakdown \(p < 0.05\). Skin inspection protocols alone did not) Tj
T*
(prevent most injuries. Device use was associated with reduced injury progression to deeper) Tj
T*
(tissue layers. These results suggest that multi-phase prevention strategies beginning in) Tj
T*
(prehospital care, combined with systematic assessment at ward admission, may improve) Tj
T*
(outcomes in this vulnerable population.) Tj
ET
